cff-version: 1.2.0
title: tapewasm
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Kansuke
    family-names: Habano
    alias: habakan
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0009-3429-9227'
abstract: >-
  Compiles a log density, written as an autodiff tape, to a WebAssembly
  module that returns the value and every partial derivative in one call,
  and samples it in the browser with nuts-rs (NUTS) or mean-field ADVI.
  Knows nothing about models: Stan (stanwasm) and PyMC (pymcwasm) front
  ends write the tape.
keywords:
  - bayesian-inference
  - webassembly
  - automatic-differentiation
  - nuts
  - rust
  - probabilistic-programming
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/habakan/tapewasm'
version: 0.3.4
date-released: "2026-09-26"
